@prefix : <https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_titleblock#> .
@prefix tb: <https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_titleblock#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/adiro/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix dm: <https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_drawing_metadata#> .

#################################################################
#    Ontology
#
#    THIS MODULE NOW DECLARES NO TERMS.
#
#    Team decision, 2026-09-14: aec_drawing_metadata is the single
#    repository for drawing metadata, so every new concept lands there
#    rather than in a parallel module. All eight terms this module held
#    were relocated to aec_drawing_metadata on that date, keeping their
#    local names:
#
#      Organization                 -> dm:Organization
#      assertsMetadataFor           -> dm:assertsMetadataFor
#      assertsClient                -> dm:assertsClient
#      assertsOriginator            -> dm:assertsOriginator
#      organizationName             -> dm:organizationName
#      dimensionUnits               -> dm:dimensionUnits
#      assertsCrossReferenceNumber  -> dm:assertsCrossReferenceNumber
#      extractionHint               -> dm:extractionHint
#
#    The asserts<Thing> naming survives the move and matters MORE in
#    the merged namespace, not less: dm:assertsClient (a claim read off
#    a printed region) and dm:isCheckedBy (a fact about a revision) now
#    sit side by side, and the prefix no longer tells them apart. The
#    verb has to.
#
#    OPEN — WHETHER THIS FILE SHOULD EXIST AT ALL.
#
#    An ontology declaring nothing still validates, but it publishes an
#    empty documentation page and invites the question this comment is
#    answering. Deleting it means also removing the catalog-v001.xml
#    entry, the generate_docs.py dependency_order entry, the mkdocs.yml
#    nav entry, changelogs/aec_titleblock.md, the display JSON and the
#    generated docs/ artefacts. That was NOT part of the relocation
#    decision, so the file is kept pending an explicit call — see
#    docs/modularization/aec_titleblock-build-plan.md §1d.
#
#    The withdrawal record below is retained deliberately. It is the
#    reasoning for terms that were considered and rejected, which is
#    the most expensive thing to rediscover, and it is not duplicated
#    in aec_drawing_metadata.
#################################################################

<https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_titleblock> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "AEC Titleblock Ontology" ;
    rdfs:comment "Retired placeholder. Every term formerly declared here was relocated to aec_drawing_metadata on 2026-09-14 by team decision, that module being the single repository for drawing metadata. This file declares no terms and is retained only for its record of vocabulary considered and rejected; whether it should be deleted outright is an open question." ;
    dcterms:title "AEC Titleblock Ontology" ;
    dcterms:description "Retired placeholder. Every term formerly declared here was relocated to aec_drawing_metadata on 2026-09-14 by team decision, that module being the single repository for drawing metadata. This file declares no terms and is retained only for its record of vocabulary considered and rejected; whether it should be deleted outright is an open question." ;
    dcterms:license <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html> ;
    dcterms:creator "Buro Happold — Machine Learning R&D" ;
    dcterms:publisher "Buro Happold" ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_titleblock/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/adiro/aec_drawing_metadata> .


#################################################################
#    NOT MINTED — the record of what was considered and rejected
#
#    Retained through the 2026-09-14 relocation because none of it is
#    carried in aec_drawing_metadata. Nothing below is a term; this is
#    reasoning, kept so it is not re-derived.
#
#    (a) RESOLVED 2026-08-19 (Option 1) — reuse dm: directly, no
#        separate term. These are NOT missing; they already exist in
#        aec_drawing_metadata:
#          identificationNumber   use dm:drawingIdentifier   (DrawingSheet)
#          title                  use dm:drawingTitle        (DrawingSheet)
#          scale                  use dm:hasScale            (DrawingSheet)
#          paperSize              use dm:sheetSize           (DrawingSheet)
#          revisionIndex          use dm:revisionCode        (DrawingRevision)
#          dateOfIssue            use dm:issueDate           (DrawingRevision)
#          createdBy              use dm:isAuthoredBy        (DrawingRevision -> Person)
#          checkedBy              use dm:isCheckedBy         (DrawingRevision -> Person)
#          approvedBy             use dm:isApprovedBy        (DrawingRevision -> Person)
#          status                 use dm:hasStatusCode       (DrawingRevision -> StatusCode)
#        Extraction writes these directly onto dm:DrawingSheet /
#        dm:DrawingRevision. There is no "unvalidated claim" staging
#        layer for them — that trade-off was accepted explicitly, not
#        by default. The 2026-09-14 relocation makes this decision
#        moot in one sense (there is no longer a second module to
#        duplicate into) but the reasoning still explains why no
#        dm:asserts* twin exists for these ten.
#
#    (a2) Withdrawn after review of PR #66 (2026-08-13):
#          hasLegalOwner          Alessio Lombardi and Tianyang Huang both
#                                 observe that a title block does not
#                                 normally express legal ownership. Deferred
#                                 pending the field-frequency survey; under
#                                 the agreed <40%-of-sheets rule it is
#                                 unlikely to return. ISO 7200 §5.1.2 defines
#                                 it, but the standard is not the evidence —
#                                 the drawings are.
#          DocumentType,
#          DocumentTypeScheme,
#          hasDocumentType        Withdrawn to a later pass, to land complete.
#                                 A controlled vocabulary with no concepts in
#                                 it cannot be used, which was the review
#                                 objection, and the definition needed
#                                 tightening. Populating it also touches the
#                                 standards-licensing question (listing DIN
#                                 1356-1 Planart values), which is worth
#                                 deciding rather than rushing.
#
#    (a3) Withdrawn 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-14, after the four-project
#         field survey (docs/modularization/titleblock-field-survey-2026-09.md).
#         None appeared in ANY of the four sampled projects, so none
#         clears the agreed <40%-of-sheets rule. All were minted from a
#         standards reading rather than from drawings — exactly the
#         basis the hasLegalOwner withdrawal rejected above ("the
#         standard is not the evidence — the drawings are"):
#          supplementaryTitle     ISO 7200 §5.2.3 (optional there). Stacked
#                                 title lines do occur, but no surveyed sheet
#                                 separated them into a distinct field; the
#                                 surveyed title fields map to dm:drawingTitle.
#          numberOfSheets,
#          sheetNumber            ISO 7200 §5.1.7 and §5.1.6 — the 'Sheet 3
#                                 of 7' pair. numberOfSheets went 2026-09-11
#                                 and sheetNumber followed 2026-09-14, so the
#                                 sheet-position concept is absent ENTIRELY
#                                 rather than half-modelled. Note §5.1.6 is
#                                 MANDATORY in ISO 7200 — this is a deliberate
#                                 departure from the standard on the grounds
#                                 that the sampled drawings do not print it,
#                                 not an oversight.
#          planKey                DIN SPEC 91391-1 Plankopf composite code. A
#                                 German-practice field; the surveyed corpus
#                                 is UK/US projects, so it may well return
#                                 when German projects are sampled. Withdrawn
#                                 as unevidenced, NOT as wrong.
#
#    (b) Dropped as redundant, per the vocabulary review — do not add:
#          Sheet                  use dm:DrawingSheet
#          Discipline             use dcommon:Discipline (a class hierarchy,
#                                 which gives sub-discipline rollup that a flat
#                                 SKOS scheme would lose). NOTE: referencing it
#                                 needs an owl:imports of aec_domain_common,
#                                 which would pull the whole module chain — the
#                                 import question is unresolved, so nothing
#                                 references dcommon: yet.
#          hasNorthPointOrientation   use UC-07 northArrowAngle (drawing-level)
#          hasAnnotationBlock     use dm:Legend / dm:Note with dm:contains
#          pageNumber/numberOfPages   duplicated the sheet-position pair,
#                                 itself withdrawn entirely in (a3) above
#
#    (c) Later passes: the remaining SKOS schemes and their concepts; the
#        extension properties; and the extraction-provenance layer, which is
#        blocked on the RDF-star vs reification decision. An extraction
#        timestamp must be included when that lands — its absence was a real
#        gap found by comparison with DANO. All of these now target
#        aec_drawing_metadata rather than this module.
#
#    (d) Parked 2026-09-01, pending a team discussion on shape: the
#        organisation-role gap found in all four surveyed projects —
#        assertsContractor, assertsEngineer, assertsArchitect,
#        assertsConsultant. dm:assertsOriginator covers the general case
#        for now. See the survey doc §3.1, §5.
#################################################################
